# Environments: <service>

One row per GitHub environment. Settings live in the repository or
organization settings (or in infrastructure code that manages them); this file
records the intended values so a reviewer can compare.

| Setting | dev | test | production |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Purpose | integration on every trunk commit | release candidate checks | users |
| Deploys from | `ci` on `main` | after dev succeeds | after test succeeds |
| Deployment branches and tags | `main` | `main` | `main` |
| Required reviewers | none | none | release approvers team (max six entries) |
| Prevent self-review | n/a | n/a | on |
| Wait timer | 0 | 0 | optional, minutes |
| Allow administrators to bypass | n/a | n/a | off |
| Custom protection rules | none | none | change-window or monitoring app, if used |
| Environment variables | `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, `AZURE_TENANT_ID`, `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`, `AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP` | same names, test values | same names, production values |
| Environment secrets | none (OIDC) | none (OIDC) | none (OIDC) |
| Entra application or managed identity | `orders-deploy-dev` | `orders-deploy-test` | `orders-deploy-prod` |
| Federated subject | `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:dev` | `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:test` | `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:production` |
| Azure role and scope | role that updates the app, on dev resources only | same on test | narrowest role that updates the app, on the production app only |
| Rollout strategy | replace | blue-green by label | canary 10, 50, 100 with bake |
| Rollback target kept | 1 previous revision | 1 previous revision | previous revision active at 0% |
| Smoke check | `/healthz` | `/healthz` plus API checks | `/healthz` plus synthetic journeys |

## Rules

- Names are case-insensitive in concurrency groups; keep one spelling.
- An identity serves exactly one environment; never reuse the production
  identity elsewhere.
- Changing a protection rule is a reviewed change with an owner.
- Repositories created after 2026-07-15 use the immutable subject format
  `repo:<owner>@<owner-id>/<repo>@<repo-id>:environment:<name>`; match the
  federated credential to the format the repository actually emits.
